\subsection*{Tool 24 — Jordan Curve Theorem}
The Jordan Curve Theorem states that the complement of a simple closed curve has exactly two components. It also implies that if \(\operatorname{int}(\gamma)\subset U,\)
where \(U\) is some open set, then \(\gamma\) is null-homotopic in \(U\).

